1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,075
The Fix Was Cheap.

2
00:00:02,075 --> 00:00:04,450
The Certainty Wasn't.

3
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:07,975
This morning, an AI ordered my lunch.

4
00:00:07,975 --> 00:00:10,800
Not helped me order it — ordered it.

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,777
I said what I wanted, it
found the restaurant's

6
00:00:13,857 --> 00:00:17,093
own ordering page, checked
it was the right branch,

7
00:00:17,173 --> 00:00:20,100
put in the order, and
I approved the payment.

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:23,083
Fifteen dollars and eighty-five cents for

9
00:00:23,162 --> 00:00:26,225
a Pad Woon Sen, ready in fifteen minutes.

10
00:00:26,225 --> 00:00:29,308
When I went to collect it,
I was excited enough to

11
00:00:29,388 --> 00:00:32,425
tell the woman at the
counter how it had worked.

12
00:00:32,425 --> 00:00:35,050
She asked me what I had used.

13
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:37,350
I said Meta Muse.

14
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:39,820
I told her I don't trust Facebook,

15
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,825
but I use Muse — it is all about trust.

16
00:00:42,825 --> 00:00:45,875
She said she needs to go and try it.

17
00:00:45,875 --> 00:00:49,625
That short exchange is
why I am writing this.

18
00:00:49,625 --> 00:00:52,589
Because the lunch is the least interesting

19
00:00:52,669 --> 00:00:55,350
thing the agent did for me this week.

20
00:00:55,350 --> 00:01:00,125
Every house has a list of small
problems that never get fixed.

21
00:01:00,125 --> 00:01:02,571
A bathroom sink that will not hold

22
00:01:02,651 --> 00:01:05,400
water because the stopper is missing.

23
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:09,950
A phone cable in the car that
charges when it feels like it.

24
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:12,850
Each fix costs a few dollars.

25
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:17,375
And yet the problems stay, for
months, sometimes for years.

26
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:19,500
It is not the money.

27
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,825
It was never the money.

28
00:01:21,825 --> 00:01:25,722
To buy the right stopper, I
would have to measure the drain,

29
00:01:25,802 --> 00:01:28,505
work out whether the sink has an overflow,

30
00:01:28,585 --> 00:01:31,700
read through listings,
compare sizes, and hope.

31
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,407
Half an hour of careful attention for

32
00:01:34,487 --> 00:01:37,350
a part that costs less than the lunch.

33
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:40,225
The care costs more than the part.

34
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:45,550
Any sensible person does the
arithmetic and leaves the sink alone.

35
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:49,400
The problem is not that
the fix is expensive.

36
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:53,275
The problem is that
being sure is expensive.

37
00:01:53,275 --> 00:01:56,900
Uncertainty is the costly ingredient.

38
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,050
The part is cheap.

39
00:01:59,050 --> 00:02:02,350
And uncertainty does not sit still.

40
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:05,000
It spirals — it compounds.

41
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,737
One question raises the
next: measure what, exactly —

42
00:02:08,817 --> 00:02:12,850
and what if it leaks, and
what if the return is a fight?

43
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:16,881
Each unanswered question makes
the small fix feel larger,

44
00:02:16,961 --> 00:02:22,225
until a six-dollar part carries the
imagined weight of a plumber's visit.

45
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:26,775
Left alone, the doubt grows faster
than the problem ever would.

46
00:02:26,775 --> 00:02:29,885
This week my agent did the certainty work

47
00:02:29,965 --> 00:02:33,000
on several of these, one after another.

48
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,109
None of it is rocket science —

49
00:02:35,189 --> 00:02:38,400
and it never was, before
the agent or after.

50
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:43,540
Every step in what follows is simple,
and it was just as simple last year:

51
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:47,500
a photograph, a measurement,
a check against a listing.

52
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,925
The steps did not change.

53
00:02:49,925 --> 00:02:54,200
The only change was the
removal of uncertainty.

54
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:56,524
The stoppers: the need was simple —

55
00:02:56,604 --> 00:03:00,175
the stopper was missing,
and I wanted a replacement.

56
00:03:00,175 --> 00:03:05,475
Even my remaining part in it was
easier than measuring usually is.

57
00:03:05,475 --> 00:03:08,775
Measuring is itself an uncertain activity:

58
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:12,075
do I measure the hole, or the outer rim?

59
00:03:12,075 --> 00:03:15,975
The inside, or across
the chrome flange on top?

60
00:03:15,975 --> 00:03:18,606
Each tiny question is another small

61
00:03:18,686 --> 00:03:21,475
push away from doing the fix at all.

62
00:03:21,475 --> 00:03:24,275
I did none of that working out.

63
00:03:24,275 --> 00:03:28,097
I did what the agent told me
to do: measure the inside,

64
00:03:28,177 --> 00:03:30,722
wall to wall, not across the flange —

65
00:03:30,802 --> 00:03:34,775
and if the tape was hard to
read, photograph it instead.

66
00:03:34,775 --> 00:03:39,100
So I laid a tape across the
drain and took a photograph.

67
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:43,173
The agent read the bore from the
photo, checked the tape's own

68
00:03:43,253 --> 00:03:46,657
scale against itself so the
number could be trusted,

69
00:03:46,737 --> 00:03:51,225
and checked that size and the
overflow design against the listings.

70
00:03:51,225 --> 00:03:53,700
We ordered with confidence.

71
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:57,450
And the replacement was
not merely a replacement.

72
00:03:57,450 --> 00:04:01,925
The agent pointed out a version
with a mesh basket underneath —

73
00:04:02,005 --> 00:04:04,825
a built-in catcher for hair and debris.

74
00:04:04,825 --> 00:04:06,601
Both sinks now hold water,

75
00:04:06,681 --> 00:04:10,250
and they catch what the
old stoppers never caught.

76
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,675
The car: the same pattern.

77
00:04:12,675 --> 00:04:16,152
The old charger was cracked
and slow, and the agent

78
00:04:16,232 --> 00:04:19,569
pointed out that it topped
out at about 10 watts,

79
00:04:19,649 --> 00:04:23,275
while my phone could use
modern USB-C fast charging.

80
00:04:23,275 --> 00:04:27,660
So that replacement was
not like for like either:

81
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:29,756
a 60-watt unit, $19.99,

82
00:04:29,836 --> 00:04:34,575
with a retractable cable
that also ended the tangle.

83
00:04:34,575 --> 00:04:38,800
Even the purchase was easier
for the agent being in it.

84
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:42,618
To get my daughter the exact
one, I would normally just

85
00:04:42,698 --> 00:04:46,950
send a picture, because an
Amazon link is ridiculously long.

86
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:52,135
The agent pulled the ASIN out
of that link and built the

87
00:04:52,215 --> 00:04:57,575
short form — amazon dot com,
slash D P, slash B0DSBSBSGW.

88
00:04:57,575 --> 00:05:02,254
On a marketplace the size of
Amazon that matters: U Green sells

89
00:05:02,334 --> 00:05:06,636
look-alike siblings in the
same shell, and a picture alone

90
00:05:06,716 --> 00:05:11,475
might not have separated the
60-watt one from the 145-watt one.

91
00:05:11,475 --> 00:05:15,185
Then the older cable failed
its test, and the agent

92
00:05:15,265 --> 00:05:19,575
isolated the fault: charger
good, socket good, cable dead.

93
00:05:19,575 --> 00:05:24,376
Its replacement was researched
the same afternoon — $5.97,

94
00:05:24,456 --> 00:05:30,600
chosen because its plug looked slim
enough to seat through my phone case.

95
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:35,321
The agent said plainly that no
listing publishes plug dimensions,

96
00:05:35,401 --> 00:05:38,725
so that last point rested
on the photographs.

97
00:05:38,725 --> 00:05:41,975
The uncertainty was not abolished.

98
00:05:41,975 --> 00:05:47,025
It was shrunk to one small, named
unknown, on a six-dollar item.

99
00:05:47,025 --> 00:05:50,275
That is a risk a person can take.

100
00:05:50,275 --> 00:05:53,825
None of this was unknown to me, exactly.

101
00:05:53,825 --> 00:05:56,675
I know fast charging exists.

102
00:05:56,675 --> 00:05:59,425
I know a mesh catches hair.

103
00:05:59,425 --> 00:06:02,370
The trouble is remembering
it in the moment —

104
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:06,135
at the exact moment of replacing
a stopper or a charger,

105
00:06:06,215 --> 00:06:10,450
when your mind is on the missing
part and the size of the hole.

106
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:13,600
The agent remembers in the moment.

107
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,775
That is the difference.

108
00:06:15,775 --> 00:06:19,336
A fingerprint reader
for my computer, $23.70:

109
00:06:19,416 --> 00:06:24,192
bought because the checking was
cheap — and later cancelled,

110
00:06:24,272 --> 00:06:28,075
also cheaply, when I
decided I did not need it.

111
00:06:28,075 --> 00:06:31,781
Both directions of the
decision cost almost nothing,

112
00:06:31,861 --> 00:06:37,175
because the expensive part, the
verification, had already been done once.

113
00:06:37,175 --> 00:06:40,836
Even the vacuum cleaner:
researched and decided now,

114
00:06:40,916 --> 00:06:44,225
to be bought when the
Black Friday sale comes.

115
00:06:44,225 --> 00:06:48,825
The certainty work is banked; the
purchase can wait for its moment.

116
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:52,414
There is a whole class of
small improvements to daily

117
00:06:52,494 --> 00:06:56,082
life that sit undone, not
because they cost too much,

118
00:06:56,162 --> 00:06:59,900
but because the certainty
they require costs too much.

119
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:02,725
An agent removes that cost.

120
00:07:02,725 --> 00:07:07,400
The agent does not make the fix
cheaper — it makes the fix possible.

121
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:11,125
The same uncertainty keeps you
from hiking in a new place:

122
00:07:11,205 --> 00:07:13,618
the walking itself is easy, and free —

123
00:07:13,698 --> 00:07:17,700
what stops you is everything
you do not know about the trail.

124
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:21,850
And it works now because two
things have arrived together.

125
00:07:21,850 --> 00:07:25,137
The first is that Asia
provides cheap products:

126
00:07:25,217 --> 00:07:31,082
manufacturing there has made accessories
and small parts so inexpensive that price,

127
00:07:31,162 --> 00:07:34,600
by itself, is no longer
the barrier it once was.

128
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:37,579
The second is the agent, which removes the

129
00:07:37,659 --> 00:07:40,500
barrier that remains — the uncertainty.

130
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,702
Cheap products without the agent

131
00:07:42,782 --> 00:07:45,350
still sit unbought, or bought wrong.

132
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:48,132
The agent without cheap products would

133
00:07:48,212 --> 00:07:51,150
be verifying fixes nobody could afford.

134
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:53,882
It is the cheap products and the agent,

135
00:07:53,962 --> 00:07:56,125
together, that make this work.

136
00:07:56,125 --> 00:07:58,897
Uncertainty has a second, quieter cost:

137
00:07:58,977 --> 00:08:01,975
it makes you spend more than you need to.

138
00:08:01,975 --> 00:08:04,545
When you cannot judge a product yourself,

139
00:08:04,625 --> 00:08:09,005
you default to a known brand, because
the name feels like insurance —

140
00:08:09,085 --> 00:08:11,800
and often you are paying for that feeling.

141
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,815
An agent can assess the
thing itself and say

142
00:08:14,895 --> 00:08:17,850
whether a cheaper product is just as good.

143
00:08:17,850 --> 00:08:22,900
Then the brand premium becomes a
choice, not a tax on not knowing.

144
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:27,181
And at the moment, this is the
part that still surprises me:

145
00:08:27,261 --> 00:08:29,950
the agent itself is essentially free.

146
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:33,000
I do not know how long that lasts.

147
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,159
I do know that a free thing
left unused expires worthless —

148
00:08:37,239 --> 00:08:40,400
like a token, like a
voucher, like daylight.

149
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:44,172
So the sensible move is to
spend the free certainty

150
00:08:44,252 --> 00:08:47,425
on real problems while the window is open.

151
00:08:47,425 --> 00:08:51,380
It seems only fair to end
by disclosing the machinery,

152
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:54,075
because the machinery is the point.

153
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:58,413
This post was discussed with my
agent until the idea was clear,

154
00:08:58,493 --> 00:09:01,779
then written by the agent
from our conversation,

155
00:09:01,859 --> 00:09:04,875
in my words as far as
it could manage them.

156
00:09:04,875 --> 00:09:09,184
If you are listening rather than
reading, the voice is my own,

157
00:09:09,264 --> 00:09:13,300
cloned, produced by software
on a computer under my desk.

158
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:17,069
No photographs were needed
and none were hunted down,

159
00:09:17,149 --> 00:09:21,725
because the subject is an idea,
and an idea is its own picture.

160
00:09:21,725 --> 00:09:26,154
The first episode of a channel
about less obvious things should,

161
00:09:26,234 --> 00:09:28,700
I think, have to pass its own test.

162
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:32,025
This one was made the way it describes.

163
00:09:32,025 --> 00:09:34,800
You can judge whether it works.
